    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0029" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v23p1/pg1"/>

                <head>1. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Japan<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1955-01-04T16:13:00-05:00">January 4, 1955—4:13
                            p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>1333. Sebald asked Ambassador Iguchi come in receive Department’s comments
                    Yoshida proposal “high command” Southeast Asia to seize anti-communist
                    propaganda offensive.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1-f2"/> Sebald said we greatly
                    appreciate Japanese interest concerting with US and other nations this purpose
                    but believe proposal would conflict Manila Pact. Suggested informal high-level
                    bilateral consultative body Tokyo already proposed by US might serve similar
                    purpose more effectively.</p>
                <p>Iguchi said mid-December UK has responded Yoshida proposal by suggesting
                    trilateral or quadrilateral (including France) consultative body Tokyo to
                    exchange information re Communist activities and <pb facs="0030" n="2"
                        xml:id="pg2"/> perhaps develop plans counter them. Sebald said initiative
                    might be left Japanese Foreign Office develop this idea further.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d1-f3"/> Memo conversation<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1-f4"/>
                    pouched.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d1-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 790.5/1–455. Confidential. Drafted
                    and approved in NA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1-f2" n="3" xml:id="d1-f2-content">
                <p>See the U.S. summary minutes of a meeting held November 9, 1954, and McClurkin’s
                    memorandum of a conversation held December 30, 1954, both in <ref
                        target="frus1952-54v14p2#pg_1779"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
